    <figcaption>Seed house at the experiment station</figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<p>The laboratory's research into feeding, breeding, and management practices also improved dairy herds. Although the dairy program ended in 1955, participating farms in Morton and Emmons counties continued to lead the state in dairy production.</p>

<p>Congress withdrew funding for agricultural research in 1935, during the Great Depression. Mandan business leaders enlisted more than 4,000 recipients of windbreak trees to contact Congress, and the laboratory's appropriation was restored. Funding was removed from the federal budget again in 1996 and 1997. Farmers and ranchers again mobilized to save the laboratory, and its funding was restored.</p>

